WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:02.870
Hi, I am Ayush Suryawanshi.

2
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:07.600
I'm a chemical engineer, and my work runs from catalyst powder to process decisions.

3
00:00:07.990 --> 00:00:11.970
I studied chemical engineering at the Indore Institute of Science and Technology,

4
00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:14.900
then did a master's in catalysis at IIT Madras,

5
00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.890
with a research semester at NTNU in Norway.

6
00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:21.070
Today, I'm a Management Trainee at LOXIM Industries.

7
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.120
It starts in the lab.

8
00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:24.840
For my thesis, I added bismuth to platinum

9
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:29.460
to help it resist carbon monoxide poisoning in formic acid fuel cells,

10
00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:32.670
and tested whether a quinone mediator could help further.

11
00:00:32.690 --> 00:00:36.840
In Norway, when the synthesis proved unsafe to scale, I reworked it.

12
00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.310
Then I put it all to the test.

13
00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:43.530
My best catalyst kept nearly 93% of its current after an hour.

14
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:46.180
Commercial platinum? About 58%.

15
00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:49.120
The quinone didn't help, and that was worth knowing too.

16
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.160
Alongside my thesis in Norway,

17
00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:54.300
I worked on a separate team project with industry partners:

18
00:00:54.310 --> 00:00:56.570
a retrofit to cut nitrogen-oxide emissions from a biomass boiler,

19
00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:01.750
from kinetic models to equipment sizing, safety and cost.

20
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.530
I presented it at an industry conference in Oslo.

21
00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.000
At LOXIM, I led a two-month study on a high-sulphate dye effluent.

22
00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:12.380
I mapped where the treatment cost goes, compared electrochemical,

23
00:01:12.390 --> 00:01:14.840
membrane and crystallisation routes with suppliers,

24
00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:18.860
and proposed a treatment train that turns the waste salt into a product,

25
00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:22.110
at about two-thirds lower modelled operating cost.

26
00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:27.040
Through all of it, I try to be clear about what a result can, and can't, show,

27
00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:30.280
whether it comes from a half-cell, a model, or a plant.

28
00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:34.150
If you're working on catalysts, electrochemistry or process design,

29
00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.440
I'd be glad to connect.

30
00:01:35.450 --> 00:01:36.300
Let's talk.
